# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored — never commit real secrets.

# --- ESPN, account 1 (private leagues 6012 and 485267278) ---
# From fantasy.espn.com browser cookies (DevTools -> Application -> Cookies).
# swid MUST keep its curly braces.
ESPN_SWID={XXXXXXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXXXXXXXXXX}
ESPN_S2=

# --- ESPN, account 2 (private league 73131979, "Green Hope Dog Walkers") ---
# A SECOND ESPN ACCOUNT, and the two are strictly disjoint: account 1 returns 401 on
# 73131979, and account 2 returns 401 on 6012 and 485267278. Measured 2026-09-05 in both
# directions, with a bad-league-id control returning 400 rather than 401 -- so the 401
# means "exists and is private", not "wrong id".
#
# Both accounts live here at once, and the LEAGUE decides which pair it reads:
# leagues/espn_green_hope.toml sets espn_swid_env / espn_s2_env to the two names below.
# A league that says nothing gets ESPN_SWID / ESPN_S2 above, so nothing else changed.
#
# This replaced a procedure where you exported one account's cookies into a shell and
# launched the editor from that exact terminal. That gave one process one account, so
# every OTHER league 401'd for as long as the shell lived, and it had to be re-established
# correctly under time pressure before a draft. Do not go back to it.
#
# None of this applies in Kubernetes: each pod's Secret supplies ESPN_SWID / ESPN_S2
# directly and secretKeyRef decides the account, so a container never sees these names.
ESPN_SWID_ESPN2={XXXXXXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXXXXXXXXXX}
ESPN_S2_ESPN2=

# --- MCP server ---
# audible exposes itself to Claude over MCP; it never calls a model, so there is no
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY here and there will not be one.
#
# Leave MCP_AUTH_TOKEN EMPTY. Authentication is not the app's job: the public route
# (mcp-audible.havenhomelab.org) is gated by mcp-auth-proxy with GitHub OAuth, the same
# as the other eight connectors, and the LAN address is open by design. This is kept
# only as an optional extra layer if you ever expose the app directly.
MCP_AUTH_TOKEN=
